# Verani Client Layer

## VeraniClient

```ts
import { VeraniClient } from "verani/client";

const client = new VeraniClient("wss://example.com/ws?userId=123");
client.on("event.name", (data) => { ... });
client.emit("event.name", payload);
```

- Uses `ConnectionManager`, `ConnectionHandler`, `MessageQueue`, `KeepaliveManager`, `EventEmitter` internally
- Protocol: `encodeClientMessage` / decode in `protocol.ts`
- Options: `VeraniClientOptions` (reconnection, keepalive, etc.)

## Examples

- `examples/server.ts` — Connection definition, room handlers, event handlers
- `defineConnection` + `createConnectionHandler` for backend; `createRoomHandler` for rooms
- Extract userId from request (`?userId=`, `?token=user:xxx`) before routing to ConnectionDO
